silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_05_glue_as_kleisli_arrow_concrete_anchor_2 silm:hasExample "In 'GlueKleisliAnchorMittens', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, Mittens is the colimit apex colim(D_Mittens) produced by the glue Kleisli arrow when all ten typed legs are present and compatible. Mittens is not a summary, not a label, and not a selected row. It is the canonical object produced by the universal property of the cocone. No competing cocone target (e.g., VetCarePlan77) replaces it; VetCarePlan77 receives the unique mediating arrow u from Mittens, confirming Mittens as the colimit.." .
